\title{peopleparser: Parse Raw Person Names into Structured Components}
\description{
Converts raw text names into structured components (salutation, first name, middle name, last name, suffix, and status) and infers gender using U.S. Census name-frequency data. Proper name ordering is disambiguated probabilistically based on how often each token appears in the first-name versus last-name position. First names can be linked to their formal names, nicknames and spelling variants, and reduced to one canonical form, using a variant table observed in Form 990 filings.
